  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "$\\,$ $n<0\\text{ or }m>-5.$\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$n<0\\text{ or }m>-5$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(n<0\\text{ or }m>-5) & ≡¬(n<0∨m>-5) \\\\  & ≡¬(n<0)∧¬(m>-5) \\\\  & ≡n\\ge 0∧m\\le -5 \\\\  & ≡n\\ge 0\\text{ and }m\\le -5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
